  "claim": "Compare selected resources at the same cohort cutoff, allowing different disclosed estimate dates. Nominal reporting-envelope matching requires equal reporting extent, category, quantity, ore moisture and declared cutoff family and canonical level. TREO grade and mass further require an explicit equal oxide sum. Strict operational equivalence also requires matched cutoff definitions (including analytical particle size for HM, basket for TREO) and explicit boundary operator. No claim of common mining economics.",
  "metric_concepts": {
    "TREO": "source-labelled total rare-earth oxide",
    "TREO_MINUS_CE": "source-labelled rare-earth oxide excluding cerium",
    "HM": "total heavy minerals",
    "TVHM": "total valuable heavy minerals",
    "MZ_EQ": "monazite equivalent",
    "NDPR": "source-labelled NdPr",
    "NB2O5": "niobium pentoxide",
    "P2O5": "phosphorus pentoxide",
    "AUD_PER_T": "AUD per tonne mine gate value",
    "USD_PER_T": "USD per tonne value"
  },
  "level_units": "Mass fractions as ppm. Currency per tonne kept in its own currency. Levels compared only within the same nominal metric.",
